1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,776
Constraint injection tests whether
the delivery plan can adapt.

2
00:00:03,846 --> 00:00:09,691
Revisit the frame, uncertainty, authority, and
smallest useful action when conditions change.

3
00:00:09,761 --> 00:00:13,324
A new restriction does not
justify bypassing controls.

4
00:00:13,394 --> 00:00:17,277
Choose a permitted fallback and
state which claims it can still test.

5
00:00:17,347 --> 00:00:20,909
Record the change, its effect
on evidence, and the next gate.

6
00:00:20,979 --> 00:00:26,569
A synthetic fallback can test workflow design
but cannot prove a production integration now

7
00:00:26,639 --> 00:00:27,727
unavailable.

8
00:00:27,797 --> 00:00:30,165
Priya prohibits external model calls.

9
00:00:30,235 --> 00:00:34,480
Luis reports the customer API
will be unavailable this week.

10
00:00:34,550 --> 00:00:36,491
The sponsor still wants progress.

11
00:00:36,561 --> 00:00:41,191
The rule-based synthetic prototype
can continue testing review behavior.

12
00:00:41,261 --> 00:00:46,039
Pause the video and complete this exercise
before opening the worked response.

13
00:00:46,109 --> 00:00:51,635
Revise the plan while preserving a useful
experiment and an honest evidence boundary.

14
00:00:51,705 --> 00:00:53,945
Use the local dataset and rules.

15
00:00:54,015 --> 00:00:57,812
Test usability, category
logic, validation, and logging.

16
00:00:57,882 --> 00:01:01,615
Mark production integration
and model benefit untested.

17
00:01:01,685 --> 00:01:04,843
Keep a future integration
gate with Luis and Priya.

18
00:01:04,913 --> 00:01:10,523
This fallback creates progress without pretending
it exercised the blocked customer systems.

19
00:01:10,593 --> 00:01:12,620
What can a synthetic fallback prove?

20
00:01:12,690 --> 00:01:15,847
A. Selected behavior within the simulation B.

21
00:01:15,917 --> 00:01:17,901
Customer API readiness C.

22
00:01:17,971 --> 00:01:19,678
Production access approval.

23
00:01:19,748 --> 00:01:21,199
The best answer is A.

24
00:01:21,269 --> 00:01:23,509
The fallback’s scope governs its claims.
